{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "cap-btitle",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1900,
   "y": -560,
   "width": 1500,
   "height": 170,
   "text": "# GLM-5.3 — one decoder layer  \nA MoE layer that runs its own DSA indexer (L6, L10, … L74). Grey bars = tensors (0.05 px/channel, long ones clipped), boxes = operations with their weights per layer. Read top → bottom; the four middle columns run side by side."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-bnote",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -300,
   "y": -560,
   "width": 1500,
   "height": 170,
   "text": "**Layer variants.** 57 of 78 layers are *shared*: they have no indexer weights and reuse the top-2048 indices of the nearest full layer above (left two columns skipped). L0–2 use a dense SwiGLU FFN 6144→12288→6144 (226.5M) instead of the MoE. Attention, norms and residuals are identical everywhere."
  },
  {
   "id": "bx32",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -154,
   "y": -330,
   "width": 307,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl33",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 174,
   "y": -342,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`x [T, 6144] from previous layer`"
  },
  {
   "id": "bn134",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -150,
   "y": -281,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**RMSNorm** (input_layernorm)",
   "color": "3"
  },
  {
   "id": "bxn35",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -154,
   "y": -185,
   "width": 307,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
